        "content": "<p>shrayjaiswal050-design opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14796\">PR #14796</a> from <code>shrayjaiswal050-design:fix/x64-i8-imul-imm</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #14660.</p>\n<p>On x64, multiplying an i8 value by a constant currently uses mulb<br>\nand can load the constant from memory. This uses a 32-bit immediate<br>\nimul instead, which gives the same low-byte result.</p>\n<p>Byte loads remain byte-sized. Added tests for both operand orders,<br>\nwrapping results, negative constants, and inputs with unused upper bits.</p>\n<p>Tested on Windows x64:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>623 x64/runtime filetests completed successfully</li>\n<li>204 codegen unit tests passed</li>\n<li>Codegen formatting and git diff --check passed</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
